risks:
  - "machine limits: a 4000 x 3000 render holds the color frame, the line-art pass targets, the depth texture, and the decoded PNG at once. The color frame alone takes 48 MB. One run can push the browser under the 1200 MB headroom bound. The check is the labeled available MB value before each batch and the labeled render peak rss mb value after each job. The batch splits when a job passes 4200 MB."
  - "heavy-run.sh stops a job after 5400 s with exit 124. A planned longer job sets HEAVY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S and gives the reason. Exit 75 means hold, and the executor retries the batch."
  - "shared asset drift: another track changed assets/bookcase.ts and rebuilt out/bookcase/bookcase.glb while this phase started. The pre-render check records the source-build stats of every shared set piece in out/storytime/l2/unit1/batches/<batch>-assets.json. The bookcase stat must read texture size 1024."
